{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"The Novice Sivaka","html":"<article id='thag1.14'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.14 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.14 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dutiyavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Two </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Sivakasāmaṇeragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Novice Sivaka </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Upajjhāyo maṁ avaca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>My mentor said to me: </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ito gacchāma sīvaka; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“Let’s leave here, Sīvaka.” </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Gāme me vasati kāyo, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>My body lives in the village, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>araññaṁ me gato mano; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>but my mind has gone to the wilderness. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Semānakopi gacchāmi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I go there even when lying down—</span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>natthi saṅgo vijānatan”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>you can’t chain those who know. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Vanavacchassa therassa (siviko) sāmaṇero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
